' First-level saving throws, read into saving_throw_names$ and saving_throw_table%.
' First the count (6), used both as the number of category names and as the number of class groups.
' Then the category names (saving_throw_names$(1..6)): only five are present, so the sixth Read takes the first
' value.
' Then 6 rows of 5 saving throws, one row per class group (saving_throw_table%(group,category)):
' Cavalier/Paladin,
' Cleric/Druid, Fighter/Barbarian/Ranger, Magic-user/Illusionist, Thief/Assassin, Monk, each in category order
' Paralyzation, Petrification, Rod/Staff/Wand, Breath Weapon, Spell.  Because of the missing name every value
' is read one place early and the last one comes from the alignment count that follows.
Data_saving_throw_table:
Data 6,Paralyzation/Poison/Death Magic,Pertification/Polymorph,Rod/Staff/Wand,Breath Weapon,Spell,14,15
Data 16,17,17,10,13,14,16,15
Data 14,15,16,17,17,14,13,11
Data 15,12,13,12,14,16,15,13
Data 12,14,16,15
' Alignments, read into alignment_names$ and alignment_allowed!.
' First the number of alignments (alignment%, 9).  Then one record per alignment:
'   name, padded with spaces (trailing spaces removed, into alignment_names$(alignment))
'   12 flags, one per class in class-table order, 1 = the class may have the alignment
'     (alignment_allowed!(alignment,class))
